  volume       = 14,
  year	       = 2016,
  abstract     = {I argue that Cormac McCarthy's he Counselor, set
                  amid the U.S.--Mexican drug wars, critiques late
                  capitalism through self-relexive genre ilmmaking.
                  Centered on the metaphor of trash, this essay
                  connects the ilm's low-art spectacle with the drug
                  trade's entrenchment in globalization and
                  multinational capitalism. he Counselor, in efect,
                  resists cinema's central role in the culture
                  industry by tying its\enquote{trashy} plot to the
                  historically pressing narcotics crisis and the
                  twenty-irst century's accumulating trash heaps.},
}

