                  {{Proliferation}}},
  urldate      = {2023-12-12},
  abstract     = {1. The human is always already posthuman. The human
                  is the animal that relies on technology in order to
                  realize its humanity. The ``post-human'' is thus an
                  ontological category, more than a historical one.
                  The very first humans were, from this perspective,
                  as posthuman as we are today. We are ever using
                  tools and prostheses to get ahead of ourselves. This
                  perspective is known as ``originary technicity''
                  (see Bernard Stiegler, David Wills, and others). 2.
                  Politics is built into the bones of (post)human
                  culture. See, for example, the bone which one chimp
                  uses to beat the other at the beginning of
